WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
 Hello. I'm Thomas Desmond,

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.440
 demo engineer at Cloudflare,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.100
 and I want to talk about Cloudflare's AI Gateway.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.200
 The short version is it gives you

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.720
 the observability and control you need in your AI applications,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.840
 and getting started is as simple as switching a URL.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.560
 Here's an application I've got.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.200
 This is Fieldstone Support,

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.280
 a support agent for summarizing issues and drafting

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.080
 replies using an LLM, and it already works.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.080
 Here's what I think is really great,

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.840
 is the whole thing runs on Cloudflare.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.800
 The app is deployed to Cloudflare Workers,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.920
 the model runs on Workers AI, Cloudflare's inference,

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.880
 and in a minute, the gateway will be on Cloudflare too.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.360
 The app, the inference, and the gateway all on one platform.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.240
 Quick tour of the app, in the top right,

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.280
 we have a drop-down for who's signed in,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.360
 so we've got different roles for different people in our organization.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.780
 The sign-in here is simulated for the demo.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.520
 Next is the scenario presets.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.440
 These are the different presets to go into the support assistant,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.440
 so I don't have to keep typing out different support tickets and whatnot.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.360
 New session starts a fresh conversation.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.640
 On the left-hand side, we have our chat window.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.280
 On the right-hand side is the gateway inspector.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.840
 Our users would generally never see this,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.080
 but it's perfect for our demo because we want to see the model being used

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.360
 and information about the requests that's going through.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.880
 Let me send a ticket, we've got Riley,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.200
 we can have a support case,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.440
 and I can send this request through.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.720
 This is heading direct to Workers AI.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.240
 There is no gateway involved,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.280
 it's streaming our response back using the Llama 3.1 model.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.840
 This is going direct to Workers AI, direct to our inference provider.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.600
 We want to add an AI Gateway because we want that observability and control.

